{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: extract the tmp-dir/log/try-finally scaffolding into a helper**

With this PR the file reaches 12 tests, and each repeats the same ~15-line scaffold: `_createTempDir()` → build `_actionJs` → construct `CliAgent` → `run()` → read the log → `finally { tmp.delete(recursive: true) }`. A small helper would cut ~60 lines and make each new test a 5-liner:

```dart
/// Runs a CliAgent job in a fresh temp dir and returns the hook log content.
Future<String> _runAgentExpectingLog({
  required String logName,
  required String jsBody,
  String? jsName = 'hook.js',
  void Function(CliAgentParams p)? params,
}) async {
  final tmp = await _createTempDir();
  final log = '${tmp.path}/$logName';
  try {
    final js = _actionJs(tmp, jsName, jsBody);
    final p = CliAgentParams()
      ..cliCommands = ['echo done']
      ..cleanupInputFolder = false;
    params?.call(p);
    await (CliAgent(
      params: p,
      workingDirectory: tmp.path,
    )).run();
    return (await File(log).readAsString()).trim();
  } finally {
    await tmp.delete(recursive: true);
  }
}
```

The existing tests already follow this shape consistently, so the migration is mechanical and can also land as a follow-up cleanup PR. Non-blocking.
